From: mscharged-port
Subject: Native LLP64 bundle callback parameter and remaining context casts
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84
Classification: native compiler/ABI compatibility; apply after 0646.

The bundle callback is passed as a FileOpenAsyncCallback whose last parameter
is the native BundleAsyncParam (uintptr_t); its unsigned long spelling only
matched on LP64 hosts. Natively it now takes __UINTPTR_TYPE__. The remaining
SHChooseCaptains callback contexts cast through __UINTPTR_TYPE__ like 0646.

Refreshed for decomp 9046e67a: upstream named the callback
OnOnDemandFrontEndBundleLoaded and declares it with C++ linkage, so the native
definition no longer adds extern "C".

diff --git a/include/Game/AsyncLoading.h b/include/Game/AsyncLoading.h
index 7dcc9e8..098af1e 100644
--- a/include/Game/AsyncLoading.h
+++ b/include/Game/AsyncLoading.h
@@ -114,7 +114,12 @@ void BeginAsyncFrontEndResourceLoad(AsyncLoadingManager* manager);
 void BeginAsyncInGameFrontEndResourceLoad(AsyncLoadingManager* manager);
 void OnLoadingSoundBankLoaded(AudioResourceLoadOwner*, void*);
 void OnPermanentFrontEndBundleLoaded();
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_NATIVE)
+// BundleAsyncParam (nlBundleFile.h) is uintptr_t natively.
+void OnOnDemandFrontEndBundleLoaded(void*, unsigned long, __UINTPTR_TYPE__);
+#else
 void OnOnDemandFrontEndBundleLoaded(void*, unsigned long, unsigned long);
+#endif
 void InitializeStadiumViewer(AsyncLoadingManager* manager);
 
 #endif // GAME_ASYNC_LOADING_H
